//////////////////////// RED BLACK TREE - 4 PROPERTIES /////////////////////////////////

1. Every node is either Red or Black.
2. The root is always Black.
3. No two adjacent Red nodes (Red node cannot have a Red parent or Red child).
4. Every path from a node to its descendant null nodes has the same number of Black nodes.

//////////////////////// RED BLACK TREE - BIGGER EXAMPLE /////////////////////////////////

                    50(B)
                 /         \
             30(R)          70(R)
            /     \        /      \
        20(B)    40(B)  60(B)    80(B)
        /   \             \         \
    10(R)  25(R)         55(R)      90(R)

//////////////////////// CHECKING 4 PROPERTIES /////////////////////////////////

1. Every node is Red or Black -> Satisfied.
2. Root 50 is Black -> Satisfied.
3. No two adjacent Red nodes:
   30(R) -> parent 50(B), children 20(B),40(B) -> ok
   70(R) -> parent 50(B), children 60(B),80(B) -> ok
   10(R),25(R) -> parent 20(B) -> ok
   55(R) -> parent 60(B) -> ok
   90(R) -> parent 80(B) -> ok
   -> Satisfied.
4. Black height same on every path (counting Black nodes to null):
   50-30-20-10-null   = 3
   50-30-20-25-null   = 3
   50-30-40-null      = 3
   50-70-60-55-null   = 3
   50-70-60-null      = 3
   50-70-80-null      = 3
   50-70-80-90-null   = 3
   -> Satisfied.

This is a valid Red-Black Tree.

//////////////////////// RED BLACK TREE - STEPS /////////////////////////////////

1. Insert the new node using normal BST insertion rule.
2. Color the newly inserted node Red.
3. If new node is the root, color it Black.
4. Check the color of the parent node.
5. If parent is Black, no violation, insertion done.
6. If parent is Red, a violation occurs, check the uncle node.
7. If uncle is Red, recolor parent, uncle to Black and grandparent to Red, move up to grandparent and repeat check.
8. If uncle is Black or null, perform rotation based on case.
9. Case LL: Right rotate grandparent, swap colors of parent and grandparent.
10. Case RR: Left rotate grandparent, swap colors of parent and grandparent.
11. Case LR: Left rotate parent, then right rotate grandparent, swap colors.
12. Case RL: Right rotate parent, then left rotate grandparent, swap colors.
13. Always color the root Black at the end.

